@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-10
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: Shared Caddy Script Fragments
  "Reusable POSIX-sh fragments for the Caddy-touching admin scripts (bootstrap, share store, provision): script preamble with rollback hook, Caddy group access, the single idempotent Caddyfile import, managed snippet install, the validate-gated reload, apex-domain detection (Public Suffix List), and shell quoting."

  Provides:
    - setup.shellQuote @source("symbol:shellQuote")
    - setup.ManagedMarker @source("symbol:ManagedMarker")
    - setup.writeScriptPreamble @source("symbol:writeScriptPreamble")
    - setup.writeSnippetInstall @source("symbol:writeSnippetInstall")
    - setup.splitSiteScheme @source("symbol:splitSiteScheme")
    - setup.isApexDomain @source("symbol:isApexDomain")
    - setup.writeCaddyGroupAccessBlock @source("symbol:writeCaddyGroupAccessBlock")
    - setup.writeCaddyImportBlock @source("symbol:writeCaddyImportBlock")
    - setup.writeCaddyReloadBlock @source("symbol:writeCaddyReloadBlock")

  Invariants:
    - shellQuote MUST single-quote arbitrary values safely, including embedded single quotes
    - isApexDomain MUST use the Public Suffix List so multi-label TLDs (.co.uk, .com.au) classify correctly, MUST treat a leading "www." as the apex it fronts, and MUST report false for subdomains and non-domains
    - writeCaddyImportBlock MUST be idempotent (grep -qF guarded) and append-only — it MUST never rewrite the main Caddyfile beyond the single import line
    - writeSnippetInstall MUST NOT replace a snippet lacking the managed marker unless FORCE=1; it MUST then print the diff and exit 3, leaving the file untouched
    - Under FORCE=1 a hand-written snippet MUST be backed up (.bak-<timestamp>) before replacement
    - Backups and temp files MUST NOT end in .caddy, so Caddy's import glob never loads them
    - writeCaddyReloadBlock MUST gate any apply on `caddy validate`, MUST restore the previous snippet (or remove a new one) and exit non-zero without reloading when validation fails, and MUST restart (not reload) when CADDY_GROUP_CHANGED is set so a new supplementary group is picked up
    - writeCaddyReloadBlock with reload=false MUST emit only the manual steps, never an active apply
    - All fragments MUST be deterministic functions of their inputs

  OutOfScope:
    - The share vhost snippet (setup.ShareStoreScript)
    - The static site vhost snippet (setup.ProvisionScript)
    - User, group, key, or directory creation (owning scripts emit those)
    - Executing the script over SSH (cli owns --apply)

  Scenario (happy-path): Idempotent import line
    Given a snippet glob and a Caddyfile path
    When writeCaddyImportBlock renders
    Then the import line is appended only when grep -qF does not already find it

  Scenario (happy-path): Restart when group changed
    Given reload is requested
    When writeCaddyReloadBlock renders
    Then it validates first and restarts Caddy when CADDY_GROUP_CHANGED, else reloads

  Scenario (negative): Hand-written snippet
    Given an existing snippet without the managed marker
    When the install fragment runs without FORCE
    Then it prints the diff, exits 3, and the file and Caddy are untouched

  Scenario (negative): Invalid result
    Given caddy validate fails after a snippet update
    When the reload fragment runs
    Then the previous snippet is restored and Caddy is not reloaded

  Scenario (edge): Multi-label TLD apex
    Given hosts example.com, www.example.com, and example.co.uk
    When isApexDomain runs
    Then all are apex, while blog.example.com and blog.example.co.uk are not
